(2922261, 409730, 30049, '<td valign="top">That''s one small duck!  The time of day that you chose to take this photo gives it a nice warm light that works well with the wood grain of the fence (and Woody).  Even the tones of the blurred background add to the image overall.  Only complaint (minor) I have is why the duck?!  Flowers, miniature doll...something.  I know, it''s a Woody photo for crying out loud, but the duck takes <u>something</u> away from the impact - integrity maybe?  Well, it''s all tongue-in-cheek anyway.  Nicely done overall.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.  :-)</td>', 'That''s one small duck!  The time of day that you chose to take this photo gives it a nice warm light that works well with the wood grain of the fence (and Woody).  Even the tones of the blurred background add to the image overall.  Only complaint (minor) I have is why the duck?!  Flowers, miniature doll...something.  I know, it''s a Woody photo for crying out loud, but the duck takes something away from the impact - integrity maybe?  Well, it''s all tongue-in-cheek anyway.  Nicely done overall.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.  :-)', '2006-10-12 12:42:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(2922265, 409266, 66985, '<td valign="top">Excellent, but couldn''t you have called it simply ''Guilty''?</td>', 'Excellent, but couldn''t you have called it simply ''Guilty''?', '2006-10-12 12:43:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2922286, 408617, 30049, '<td valign="top">It looks so "real"!  Amazing how an inanimate human-formed object can express "emotion".  Great job of posing Woody and kudos also for a perfect background and lighting setup to go with it.  Well done!</td>', 'It looks so "real"!  Amazing how an inanimate human-formed object can express "emotion".  Great job of posing Woody and kudos also for a perfect background and lighting setup to go with it.  Well done!', '2006-10-12 12:53:04.000000', NULL, 1),
