(2924923, 408823, 47020, '<td valign="top">Are those stars added in post-processing?  They kind of look like it, but they also remind me of Tokihiro Sato''s work, and since there''s obviously other light-painting going on, I have to ask...<br/> <br/>Meanwhile, I''m finding the orientation to be unsettling, but unfortunately not in a way that feels "good" to me.  :-/  I imagine you mean it to not feel quite right, but I think with the background how it is, it leaves me just wanting to rotate the image, rather than giving me the sense of falling that you''re presumably after.  It''s interesting, though.</td>', 'Are those stars added in post-processing?  They kind of look like it, but they also remind me of Tokihiro Sato''s work, and since there''s obviously other light-painting going on, I have to ask... Meanwhile, I''m finding the orientation to be unsettling, but unfortunately not in a way that feels "good" to me.  :-/  I imagine you mean it to not feel quite right, but I think with the background how it is, it leaves me just wanting to rotate the image, rather than giving me the sense of falling that you''re presumably after.  It''s interesting, though.', '2006-10-13 06:21:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2924925, 406538, 47020, '<td valign="top">That looks like it might even be just one woody, spinning.  Cool.</td>', 'That looks like it might even be just one woody, spinning.  Cool.', '2006-10-13 06:23:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2924926, 408462, 47020, '<td valign="top">I love the background and set you chose for this.  Very nice.</td>', 'I love the background and set you chose for this.  Very nice.', '2006-10-13 06:24:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2924929, 409657, 47020, '<td valign="top">Very well executed.  I love the contrast between the pale woody and the rich color of the explored wood.</td>', 'Very well executed.  I love the contrast between the pale woody and the rich color of the explored wood.', '2006-10-13 06:25:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2924932, 409447, 47020, '<td valign="top">Wow...  Am I imagining things, or do you actually have a _model_ of an EOS-1 with that lens on it?  It''s advanced editing, so maybe it''s just a separate picture skillfully placed in, but it kind of looks like a model to me, and that''s just...  too cool for words, really.  :-)<br/> <br/>edit: never mind the advanced editing remark... I went and re-read those rules, and see that doesn''t apply.<br/> <br/>I also forgot to mention the notion that surely you don''t have such a big woody as this would have to be if it was a real camera.  Or trust the woody to hold it, if you do!  ;-)</td>', 'Wow...  Am I imagining things, or do you actually have a _model_ of an EOS-1 with that lens on it?  It''s advanced editing, so maybe it''s just a separate picture skillfully placed in, but it kind of looks like a model to me, and that''s just...  too cool for words, really.  :-) edit: never mind the advanced editing remark... I went and re-read those rules, and see that doesn''t apply. I also forgot to mention the notion that surely you don''t have such a big woody as this would have to be if it was a real camera.  Or trust the woody to hold it, if you do!  ;-)', '2006-10-13 06:32:13.000000', NULL, 1),
