(2925531, 409237, 30049, '<td valign="top">Love Toy Story (both of them).  As clever as your title is and having a technically sound image - you''re running into trouble with the DNMC crowd I''m afraid.  The challenge specifically pointed out ''Woody'' the wooden stick man in the details.<br/> <br/>BTW - you should have left the label around back IMO (and straightened out his collar).  ;^)</td>', 'Love Toy Story (both of them).  As clever as your title is and having a technically sound image - you''re running into trouble with the DNMC crowd I''m afraid.  The challenge specifically pointed out ''Woody'' the wooden stick man in the details. BTW - you should have left the label around back IMO (and straightened out his collar).  ;^)', '2006-10-13 11:12:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2925541, 409611, 30049, '<td valign="top">Sorry, but I''m missing the point of the title.  Is this some subliminal message?  You''ve done a nice job of lighting the main subjects.  They are well focused and stand out well against the black background.  The tub in the middle...???  Seems out of place.  Looks like a rubbermaid or tupperware container with a urine sample in it.  Hmmm...oh well.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'Sorry, but I''m missing the point of the title.  Is this some subliminal message?  You''ve done a nice job of lighting the main subjects.  They are well focused and stand out well against the black background.  The tub in the middle...???  Seems out of place.  Looks like a rubbermaid or tupperware container with a urine sample in it.  Hmmm...oh well.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-10-13 11:17:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(2925554, 409442, 30049, '<td valign="top">I like the idea and concept here.  A few things that jump out at me that IMO would help this.  1) It would be nice if Woody wasn''t on a stand (I know not easy to do, but it IS possible).  2) A faster shutter speed would have "frozen" the smoke.  Because the smoke is moving it appears blurred.  3) The lighting is somewhat harsh.  Probably needed it that way some to get the smoke to "light" up correctly, but the lighting on ''Woody'' is too strong IMO on the outside edges (arm, shoulder, head).<br/> <br/>Just some thoughts and comments.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'I like the idea and concept here.  A few things that jump out at me that IMO would help this.  1) It would be nice if Woody wasn''t on a stand (I know not easy to do, but it IS possible).  2) A faster shutter speed would have "frozen" the smoke.  Because the smoke is moving it appears blurred.  3) The lighting is somewhat harsh.  Probably needed it that way some to get the smoke to "light" up correctly, but the lighting on ''Woody'' is too strong IMO on the outside edges (arm, shoulder, head). Just some thoughts and comments.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-10-13 11:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(2925574, 409827, 30049, '<td valign="top">I stopped and looked at this one for a while.  It''s cute.  Honestly, I''m trying to figure out what is in the frame(s) of film next to the Woody negative.  Probably not your intent.  The color cast is also a little uncomfortable.  If you''re going to shift did you consider blue or even B/W?  Sorry, I wish I could put my finger on what isn''t pulling this off for me.  :(  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'I stopped and looked at this one for a while.  It''s cute.  Honestly, I''m trying to figure out what is in the frame(s) of film next to the Woody negative.  Probably not your intent.  The color cast is also a little uncomfortable.  If you''re going to shift did you consider blue or even B/W?  Sorry, I wish I could put my finger on what isn''t pulling this off for me.  :(  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-10-13 11:26:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(2925583, 409447, 30049, '<td valign="top">Clever idea.  Well lite, the focus is fine, and postioning of the subject is ok too.  The killer on this is the background IMO.  Some distance between the subject and the bg would have blurred it out for you and kept the bg from becoming part of the viewers interest.  JMO of course.  :)  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Clever idea.  Well lite, the focus is fine, and postioning of the subject is ok too.  The killer on this is the background IMO.  Some distance between the subject and the bg would have blurred it out for you and kept the bg from becoming part of the viewers interest.  JMO of course.  :)  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-10-13 11:28:27.000000', NULL, 1),
